1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
ProofPay — original application walkthrough. Sample mode; no live AI or payment calls.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:22,000
A fictional $300 website handoff: agreed scope, delivery evidence, and the next step.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Start from the agreed brief. Keep the milestone price fixed.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Sample rules flag gaps. A Gemini key enables the implemented AI integration.

5
00:00:46,000 --> 00:01:01,000
A form success message does not establish inbox delivery.

6
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Add a clearly labeled synthetic QA report. The delivery becomes a new version.

7
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Findings cite the supplied text. The client makes the final decision.

8
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Share the reviewed version, its supporting evidence, and the $300 price.

9
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:53,000
The client can inspect the same evidence before accepting.

10
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Acceptance records this version and amount. It does not make a payment.

11
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:17,000
The accepted milestone enables an invoice. This recording uses sample mode.

12
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Simulated payment is isolated from PayPal. No money moves.

13
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Evidence, acceptance, invoice, and sample payment remain in one activity trail.

14
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Original source in Pradhyut21/proofpay-paypal-ai-hackathon. Configure Gemini and PayPal sandbox for the real integration test.
